WEBVTT
TITLE Calculus: Limits, Extrema and Integration — GATE Visual Explainer
NOTE Timings are estimated from the lesson timeline (speaking-rate based), not measured from recorded audio.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.500
A limit asks what f(x) settles near a, not what f(a) equals.

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:15.000
Substituting here gives 0/0: the numerator is 0 and so is the denominator.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Differentiate top and bottom separately: the top becomes one over the square root, the bottom becomes 1.

4
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:30.000
At x equal to minus 3 the answer is 1 over the square root of 16, which is 0.25.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.500
Only two of the five indeterminate forms may be handed straight to L'Hopital.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:45.000
0 times infinity becomes a fraction; infinity minus infinity becomes a common denominator; 1 to the infinity takes a logarithm.

7
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.500
x to the power 1 over x is infinity to the zero; its logarithm has limit zero, so the limit is e to the zero, which is 1.

8
00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:00.000
One plus x squared times e to the minus x is infinity times zero; as a fraction it is infinity over infinity and the limit is 0.

9
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Continuous at a means three things at once: the limit exists, the value exists, and they are equal.

10
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:15.000
For a piecewise function, compute the two one-sided limits separately and then match them to the stated value.

11
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.500
GATE CSE 2026 Set 1: as x tends to 0 from above, ln of 1 over x runs off to plus infinity.

12
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:30.000
So c two must be 0, leaving c one equals 3, and c one plus c two equals 3.

13
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.500
The derivative at a point exists when the two one-sided slopes agree.

14
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:45.000
The absolute value has slope minus 1 on the left of 0 and plus 1 on the right, so there is no derivative at 0.

15
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:52.500
For f equal to the larger of x and x cubed, the formula switches wherever x cubed equals x.

16
00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:00.000
At all three crossings the slopes differ, so the answer is the set minus 1, 0 and 1.

17
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.500
The mean value theorem needs continuity on the closed interval and differentiability on the open one.

18
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Then some interior point c has slope exactly equal to the average slope across the interval.

19
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:22.500
GATE CSE 2021 Set 2: the average slope from minus 3 to 3 is f(3) minus 7, all over 6, and it equals a slope that is at most 2.

20
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:30.000
Multiplying through gives f(3) at most 19, and the straight line 2x plus 13 attains it, so 19 is the best possible bound.

21
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.500
A local extremum can occur only at a critical point or at an endpoint.

22
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:45.000
GATE CSE 2023: f prime is 3 times x plus 11 times x minus 1, so the critical points are minus 11 and 1.

23
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:52.500
The sign of f prime goes plus, minus, plus, so there is a local maximum at minus 11 and a local minimum at 1.

24
00:02:52.500 --> 00:03:00.000
The second derivative confirms it: minus 36 at minus 11 and plus 36 at 1, so statements B and D are true.

25
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:07.500
Setting the derivative to zero finds interior candidates only. On a closed interval the endpoints are candidates too.

26
00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:15.000
For 2x squared minus 2x plus 6 on the interval from 0 to 2, the vertex is at one half and its value is 5.5.

27
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:22.500
The endpoints give 6 and 10, so the maximum on the closed interval is 10, attained at x equal to 2.

28
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:30.000
A maximum need not be smooth: 1 minus the absolute value of x peaks at 0, where no derivative exists.

29
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.500
Substitution reverses the chain rule: put u equal to the inner function and du equal to its derivative times dx.

30
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:45.000
In this integral the inner function is 1 over x, and its derivative brings a minus sign.

31
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:52.500
The limits also change: from 1 over pi and 2 over pi to pi and pi over 2, and the minus sign flips their order.

32
00:03:52.500 --> 00:04:00.000
The integral of cos u from pi over 2 to pi is sine pi minus sine pi over 2, which is 0 minus 1, so the answer is minus 1.

33
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:07.500
Over an interval symmetric about zero, an odd integrand contributes exactly nothing.

34
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:15.000
GATE CSE 2023: the integrand is 4x squared y minus z cubed, over three symmetric intervals.

35
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:22.500
Both terms vanish, so the answer is 0, with no antiderivative computed at all.

36
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:30.000
Reflection works too: f(x) equals 1 minus f(2 minus x) forces the integral from 0 to 2 to equal 1.

37
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:37.500
Step one: substitute. If a number comes out, that is the limit and the work is done.

38
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:45.000
Step two: use L'Hopital only on 0/0 or infinity over infinity, and rewrite anything else into one of those two.

39
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:52.500
Step three: for extrema, list the critical points and both endpoints, evaluate at every candidate, and compare the numbers.

40
00:04:52.500 --> 00:05:00.000
Step four: before integrating, check for symmetry and for an inner derivative, and never drop the minus sign from du.

